  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Wednesday)\nIssued at 227 PM MDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nCurrent Water Vapor and upper air models show near zonal flow\naloft, with an upper low located over the four corners region. \n20Z surface analysis shows high pressure centered over Wyoming\nthis afternoon Satellite has some mid and high clouds reaching\ninto southwest and south central SD. Temperatures sit in the upper\n60s and 70s, with generally light winds out of the northwest. \nLittle change to the overall pattern is expected through the \nweek, with near-zonal to northwest flow aloft hanging around. \nMostly dry conditions are expected as well. A cold front is \nexpected Thursday, dropping temperatures 15-20 degrees from today.\nLimited moisture with this disturbance, but some light\nprecipitation will be possible Thursday into Thursday night.\nTemperatures then warm up a bit for the first half of the weekend\nbefore another boundary cools the region down again on Sunday.\nOnce again, with limited moisture advection, expect little to no\nprecipitation over the weekend. Early next week the upper ridge \nbuilds over the western CONUS, prompting a rise in temperatures to\nthe 70s and low 80s for much of next week.",
